===Pronunciation===
tet·rarch·y
* IPA: //
* {{enPR|tĕträrkē}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|tetrarchia}}, from Ancient Greek {{m|grc|τετραρχία}}, from the combining form of {{m|grc|τέτταρες}}, {{m|grc|τέσσαρες||four}} + {{m|grc|-αρχία}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|tetrarchies}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} Rule by four rulers; an empire so ruled; specifically, the system of such rule of the [[Roman Empire]] from 293-313 CE instituted by [[Diocletian]] to end the {{w|Crisis of the Third Century}}.

